---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';const b='/equipment/16-02/',herzan='https://www.herzan.com/wp-content/uploads/2015/12/Faraday-Cage-Data-Sheet.pdf',warner='https://www.warneronline.com/sites/default/files/2018-09/blm_setup.pdf#page=3';
---
<Layout pageTitle="Shielded benchtop enclosure" description="Explore an inert low-noise bench with a passive illustrative pickup comparison." wide={true}><article class="equipment" id="shieldbench"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/16-02/">← Equipment 16-02</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Register</a><a href="#shield-evidence">Reference sheet</a></nav><header class="eq-mast"><p class="eq-meta">16-02 / PASSIVE ACQUISITION FIXTURE</p><h2>What changes when the door closes?</h2><p class="eq-lede">An inert dummy input picks up a 60 Hz tone. Open and close the virtual door to compare it with an assigned 20 dB attenuation. No shielding is measured or predicted for a real enclosure.</p></header>
<div class="s-cols"><section><h3>Custom enclosure</h3><canvas id="shield-model" aria-label="Orbitable mesh enclosure with hinged door and feedthrough"></canvas><p id="shield-viewstatus" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><button id="shield-front">Whole bench / reset view</button><button id="shield-side">Feedthroughs</button><button id="shield-fixture">Dummy fixture view</button><p>Click the door handle, blue signal feedthrough or green ground lug. The hardware actions match the controls beside the viewer.</p></section>
<section><h3>Virtual coupling</h3><label>Injected peak amplitude, µV<input id="shield-input" type="number" min="1" max="10000" value="200" step="any"/></label><label>Test tone Hz<select id="shield-freq"><option>60</option><option>50</option></select></label><label>Assigned closed attenuation, dB<input id="shield-db" type="number" min="0" max="60" value="20" step="any"/></label><p id="shield-state"></p><button id="shield-door">Open door</button><button id="shield-ground">Disconnect virtual ground</button><button id="shield-feed">Disconnect signal feedthrough</button><button id="shield-reset">Restore example</button><p id="shield-status" role="status"></p><p>These are virtual state toggles, not physical grounding or wiring instructions.</p></section></div>
<section><h3>Pickup comparison</h3><canvas id="shield-chart" width="900" height="310" aria-label="Injected and connected pickup traces for first three cycles"></canvas><p id="shield-read" role="status"></p><button id="shield-export">Download voltage waveform JSON</button><button id="shield-report">Download state report JSON</button><p><a href={b+'example-waveform.json'}>Example waveform</a>. The connected output uses the site <code>bts.analog-waveform.v1</code> schema (volts, uniform seconds, synthetic provenance), accepted by the <a href="/simulations/equipment/09-04/simulator/">09-04 oscilloscope</a> (<a href={b+'scope-verification.json'}>40 µV peak-to-peak handoff check</a>). An open feedthrough means absence of a trace, not zero volts.</p></section>
<section id="shield-evidence"><h3>Reference and checks</h3><p>Original custom design, not modeled after a particular serial number. Nominal design body is 600 mm wide × 650 mm tall × 540 mm deep before handle and feedthrough projections. See the <a href={herzan}>Herzan custom enclosure brochure</a> for open/closed design context and <a href={warner}>Warner’s discussion of mesh enclosures</a> for general laboratory use. The simplified dummy fixture has no neurons or recording subject.</p><div class="s-cols"><figure><img alt="Original closed mesh cage render" src={b+'closed.webp'}/><figcaption>Original closed station. Front handle, side signal feedthrough and virtual ground are independently selectable.</figcaption></figure><figure><img alt="Original open mesh cage exposing inert dummy input" src={b+'open.webp'}/><figcaption>Original open door view. The modeled grid is representational, not a physical shielding specification.</figcaption></figure></div>
<p>For the virtual closed and grounded state, amplitude multiplier is 10<sup>−dB/20</sup>. In the open or ungrounded state this exercise assigns unity. This is a deliberately simplified model: actual coupling also depends on frequency, fit, termination, cable routing and other equipment effects. Tone peak amplitude is computed by in-phase and quadrature projection over full cycles (1,000 samples at 2 kHz). No magnetic-field shielding or physical safety claims.</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>200 µV, −20 dB</td><td>20 µV peak; 0.1×</td><td>20.000 µV peak; 0.1000×</td></tr><tr><td>Open door</td><td>Original 200 µV</td><td>200.00 µV peak</td></tr><tr><td>Remove virtual feedthrough</td><td>Missing, not zero</td><td>No trace; voltage download blocked</td></tr></tbody></table><p><a href={b+'build-model.py'}>Editable Blender source</a> · <a href={b+'shielded-bench.glb'}>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={b+'pickup.mjs'}>Pure solver and actions</a> · <a href={b+'vr.json'}>VR hit bounds and hinge</a>. No headset test claimed.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/16-02/client.mjs';</script>
<style is:global>#shieldbench .s-cols{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.13fr) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem}#shieldbench section{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);margin:1rem 0;min-width:0}#shieldbench :is(input,select,button){font:inherit;color:inherit;background:var(--panel);border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.45rem;max-width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}#shieldbench label{display:grid;gap:.2rem;min-width:0;margin:.5rem 0}#shieldbench label :is(input,select){width:100%;min-width:0}#shieldbench button{margin:.35rem .25rem .2rem 0;cursor:pointer}#shieldbench button:disabled{opacity:.5}#shieldbench button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid #b28d5e}#shield-model{display:block;width:100%;height:330px;touch-action:none}#shield-chart{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;background:#18272c}#shieldbench figure{margin:.5rem 0}#shieldbench figure img{width:100%}#shieldbench table{font-size:.9rem;border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;text-align:left}#shieldbench td,#shieldbench th{border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);padding:.35rem}#shieldbench code{overflow-wrap:anywhere}@media(max-width:780px){#shieldbench .s-cols{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1fr)}#shield-model{height:280px}}</style>
